+  && ok "build.md's Fix step still fixes CONFIRMED findings" \
+  || bad "build.md's Fix step no longer says confirmed — triage before you fix, and before you count"
+# Two-sided, because this one has regressed twice. The audit round narrowed both phase.js and build.md
+# to what is true ("both claimed the fabricated-sha hole was closed. It is not"), and the next change to
+# this file reinstated it as a guarantee. Every sha operation phase.js performs is a SHAPE test
+# (`sha()`) or an equality test against the base; the reported value is discarded in favour of the
+# gates step's real head. Nothing resolves a sha, because a Workflow script has no shell — and
+# sim-phase.js asserts only the weaker property, that a fabricated sha cannot close an EMPTY diff.
+grep -qF 'it does not detect a fabricated sha' three-loop-workflow/references/build.md \
+  && ok "build.md still records that a fabricated sha is made harmless, not detected" \
+  || bad "build.md no longer records the fabricated-sha limit — the only place in the skill it is written down"
+# CLAUSE-scoped, and it has to be, because that is where negation scopes in English. Two narrower
