+# sha" (A1-A2c, A2e-A2g), "a sha it never created" (A2h) — or when the fabrication IS the object
+# noun, whose only referent anywhere in this skill is that sha (A2d's passive, which is the wording
+# this check's own FAIL message uses). Residual, and it is the price of keeping A2d: that
+# nominalisation is unbound, so "spots the fabrication of a gate result" would still be reported.
+OBJ = r"(?:" + FAB + GAP + SHA + r"|" + SHA + GAP + FAB + r"|\bfabrications?\b|\bforger(?:y|ies)\b)"
+CLAIM = re.compile(ACT + GAP + OBJ + r"|" + OBJ + GAP + ACT
+                   + r"|\bresolv\w*" + GAP + SHA + r"|" + SHA + GAP + r"\bresolv\w*", re.I)
