+#
+# "The sentence that names it" has to mean one statement. This check split statements the same way the
+# sweep above did, so a Markdown list collapsed into one sentence here too and the marker in one bullet
+# exempted a path named in another — A3 again, through formatting. Same fix, same reason: a list item
+# is a statement without a full stop. A6b pins it.
+if python3 - <<'PYPATH'
+import io, os, re, sys
+# Any file under scripts/, at any depth, with any extension — because that is what the header and the
+# ok line both say, and because the reader is misrouted identically whatever the suffix is. The first
+# cut read `scripts/NAME.(js|sh)`, which is neither: `scripts/verify-plan.py` and
+# `scripts/lib/verify-plan.js` were never extracted, so a skill that named them printed `ok every
+# scripts/ path the shipped skill names resolves`, exit 0, zero FAIL. That is 77cda1b's defect — a
+# header claiming more than the extraction covers — one axis over. A9/A9b pin both shapes.
+# An extension is still required: `scripts/` naming the directory rather than a file is not a
+# misroute, and a bare directory has nothing to resolve.
